{"id":"capelo-ivens","title":"De Angola à Contra-Costa: Capelo and Ivens","who":"Hermenegildo Capelo & Roberto Ivens","when":"1884–1885","vehicle":"On foot, with porters","kind":"walk","color":"#166534","summary":"Two Portuguese naval officers cross Africa from the Atlantic to the Indian Ocean, from Moçâmedes in Angola to Quelimane in Mozambique: about 8,300 km in some 14 months, a third of it through land no European had mapped. The expedition backed Portugal's \"Pink Map\" claim to the lands between its colonies, and their book \"De Angola à Contra-Costa\" (1886) became a classic of exploration.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Hermenegildo Capelo","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermenegildo_Capelo"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Roberto Ivens","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roberto_Ivens"}],"approximate":"Only the main known places; the expedition's real path wound far more, and the straight lines between places are a rough guide only.","km":3307,"bbox":[12.1458,-17.8775,36.8902,-10.3964],"stops":[{"name":"Moçâmedes","place":"Moçâmedes, Angola","at":[-15.195,12.1458],"date":"1884","text":"The start on the Angolan coast, after leaving Lisbon in January 1884.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Palacio_da_Justi%C3%A7a_%2819515367551%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Palacio_da_Justi%C3%A7a_%2819515367551%29_%28cropped%29.jpg","page":"Moçâmedes","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palacio_da_Justi%C3%A7a_%2819515367551%29_%28cropped%29.jpg","credit":"David Stanley from Nanaimo, Canada","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Huíla plateau","place":"Lubango, Angola","at":[-14.9195,13.4898],"text":"Up the escarpment to the cool Huíla plateau, where the long journey inland was organised.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Lubango-Namibe_landscape.jpg/500px-Lubango-Namibe_landscape.jpg","page":"Huíla Province","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lubango-Namibe_landscape.jpg","credit":"Erik Cleves Kristensen","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Humbe","place":"Humbe, Cunene","at":[-16.68,14.9],"text":"South-east to the Cunene river, then into country barely known to Europeans.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/%C5%98eka_Kunene_River%2C_vodop%C3%A1dy_Epupa_Falls_-_Namibie%2C_Angola_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-%C5%98eka_Kunene_River%2C_vodop%C3%A1dy_Epupa_Falls_-_Namibie%2C_Angola_-_panoramio.jpg","page":"Cunene River","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C5%98eka_Kunene_River%2C_vodop%C3%A1dy_Epupa_Falls_-_Namibie%2C_Angola_-_panoramio.jpg","credit":"Pavel Špindler","license":"CC BY 3.0"}},{"name":"Garanganja (Katanga)","place":"Bunkeya","at":[-10.3964,26.9685],"text":"The lands of Msiri's powerful trading kingdom in Katanga, near the sources of the great rivers they had come to study.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Msiri_1830_1891.jpg/500px-Msiri_1830_1891.jpg","page":"Msiri","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Msiri_1830_1891.jpg","credit":"CAPELLO &amp; IVENS (H. - R.)","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Zumbo","place":"Zumbo, Mozambique","at":[-15.6161,30.445],"text":"Down to the Zambezi at the old Portuguese trading post of Zumbo."},{"name":"Tete","place":"Tete, Mozambique","at":[-16.156,33.586],"text":"Down the Zambezi to Tete.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Tetesuspensionbridge.JPG/500px-Tetesuspensionbridge.JPG","page":"Tete, Mozambique","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tetesuspensionbridge.JPG","credit":"Martha Evans, Cape Town (EmjayE2 at en.wikipedia)","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Quelimane","place":"Quelimane, Mozambique","at":[-17.8775,36.8902],"date":"21 Jun 1885","text":"The Indian Ocean coast: Angola to the \"other coast\", achieved. They were welcomed home in Lisbon by King Luís.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Cine_Teatro_Aguia_Quelimane_%289516168590%29.jpg/500px-Cine_Teatro_Aguia_Quelimane_%289516168590%29.jpg","page":"Quelimane","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cine_Teatro_Aguia_Quelimane_%289516168590%29.jpg","credit":"A Verdade from Maputo, Moçambique","license":"CC BY 2.0"}}],"legs":[{"by":"walk","km":148,"line":[[-15.195,12.1458],[-14.9195,13.4898]]},{"by":"walk","km":247,"line":[[-14.9195,13.4898],[-16.68,14.9]]},{"by":"walk","km":1479,"line":[[-16.68,14.9],[-13.8204,20.612],[-10.3964,26.9685]]},{"by":"walk","km":692,"line":[[-10.3964,26.9685],[-15.6161,30.445]]},{"by":"walk","km":341,"line":[[-15.6161,30.445],[-16.156,33.586]]},{"by":"walk","km":400,"line":[[-16.156,33.586],[-17.8775,36.8902]]}]}